  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Perimeter, area, surface area and volume — from circles and trapezia up to cylinders, cones and spheres. Read each question carefully for the value of \\( \\pi \\) it expects (often \\( 3.14 \\) or \\( \\tfrac{22}{7} \\)).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — The circle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Circumference \\( C=2\\pi r=\\pi d \\); area \\( A=\\pi r^{2} \\). An arc and sector are simply fractions of these, scaled by \\( \\dfrac{\\theta}{360} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Circle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( C=2\\pi r,\\quad A=\\pi r^{2} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cylinder",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( V=\\pi r^{2}h \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Sphere",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( V=\\tfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^{3} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Cone",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( V=\\tfrac{1}{3}\\pi r^{2}h \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Prism",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( V=A_{\\text{cross}}\\times \\ell \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Trapezium",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( A=\\tfrac12(a+b)h \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the volume of a cylinder with \\( r=3 \\) cm and \\( h=10 \\) cm. Take \\( \\pi=3.14 \\).</p>\\[ V=\\pi r^{2}h=3.14\\times 9\\times 10=282.6\\ \\text{cm}^{3}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the volume of a sphere of radius \\( 3 \\) cm. Take \\( \\pi=3.14 \\).</p>\\[ V=\\tfrac{4}{3}\\pi r^{3}=\\tfrac{4}{3}\\times 3.14\\times 27=113.04\\ \\text{cm}^{3}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
